@@ -111,3 +111,18 @@ This bridge targets upstream 0.22.0 records. Older flat/legacy actor layouts req
 migration first. Task-boundary PM handoffs are portable; live Codex receipts remain checkout-bound.
 No automatic migration of existing standalone `.deliver` runs, mid-story conversion, sprint
 planning engine or automatic integration re-verification is claimed.
+
+## Native remote completion hold
+
+A protected integration branch uses the remote lifecycle in `references/shipping.md`. Native
+remote evidence remains in the canonical integration record until its exact fetched terminal
+commit is fast-forwarded into the approved local integration checkout and adopted. During that
+interval `pm.mjs status` reports `REMOTE_PENDING`, `REMOTE_CLOSURE_PROVEN` or
+`LOCAL_ADOPTION_PENDING`; claim and direct start remain blocked. Malformed, copied or ambiguous
+records report `UNKNOWN`. A proved completed record remains readable after later legitimate
+integration commits, and completed history does not block a later story.
+
+Provider writes retain prepared, executing and observed transitions. A process restart never
+replays an ambiguous executing write merely because its PID disappeared. Read-only reconciliation
+may adopt an exact observed provider effect; same-process replay requires a positively ended call
+and exact absence proof on the same attempt token.
